{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tied-type type is used as an attribute of the tied element to specify where the visual representation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of a tie begins and ends. A tied element which joins two notes of the same pitch can be specified with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tied-type start on the first note and tied-type stop on the second note. To indicate a note should be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"undamped, use a single tied element with tied-type let-ring. For other ties that are visually attached to a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"single note, such as a tie leading into or out of a repeated section or coda, use two tied elements on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same note, one start and one stop."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Enumeration Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/Kind-swift.enum\/continue","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/Kind-swift.enum\/letRing","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/Kind-swift.enum\/start","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/Kind-swift.enum\/stop"],"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","generated":true},{"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/Kind-swift.enum\/Equatable-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documen